WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:01.734
-Welcome back, Bryan.

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:03.067
We love having you here, bud.

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.667
-Thank you.
Good to be here.

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:06.133
-You're a very busy, busy man.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:07.868
I follow you on the socials

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:09.467
and in all the media
and everything.

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:10.968
I read what you're up to.

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:13.434
You're traveling the world
or the country

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:16.267
-Yeah.
-with this Dos Hombres mezcal.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:18.434
-Yes.
-That you're doing
with Aaron Paul.

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:20.033
-Dos Hombres.
-Dos Hombres.

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:21.234
[ Cheering ]
-Yes, yes.

00:00:21.234 --> 00:00:22.534
-I mean, you're going all
over the place.

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:25.133
You surprise people
and you surprise liquor stores

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:26.100
and you just show up
and they're like...

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.334
-We do.
-..."What's going on?"

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:29.367
[ Laughter ]
-I know. It's pretty wild.

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:32.501
It's as close to, you know,
a rock tour

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:35.000
as my fantasy will allow me
to go, you know...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.834
...because we go to these places

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:41.133
and we sign bottles for fans
and things and they love it.

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:43.067
-I have a video of this
because I wanted to show this.

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:45.300
This is a video of one of the
events that you guys showed up.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.868
Look at the reaction on this.

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:48.434
-Here we go. Here we go.
Here we go. Here we go.

00:00:48.434 --> 00:00:50.100
Let's go.
-Alright, let's go!

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.701
-[ Screaming ]
-Ohhh!

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:54.334
-Dude, look at all these people.
-Wow!

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:55.434
-Look at this.

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:56.534
-[ Screaming ]

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:58.133
-Dude, that's crazy!

00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:00.234
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:01.834
That's so fun!

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:03.334
-It's so much fun.

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:06.200
And doing it with Aaron,

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.701
you know, my partner
on "Breaking Bad,"

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.167
he's such a great guy

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:12.901
and to do Dos Hombres
with him is a thrill.

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:15.701
-I was looking at something else
as I was searching online

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:19.467
for things about you and I saw
that a pair of Walter White's

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:22.334
underwear went up for auction...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:25.634
-Oh, I heard about this.
-...for $32,000.

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:29.734
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:33.000
I should mention,
these were never worn.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.400
-Those were never worn.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.901
The ones that are soiled go
for much higher.

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:40.200
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.100
Is that --
-I wish I didn't say that.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.334
[ Laughter ]
-No.

00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:47.434
But could you imagine?
30,000.

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:49.501
-I mean, people are crazy!
-Yeah!

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:51.734
-Who, in their right mind,
is buying a pair

00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:54.400
of tighty-whitey underwears
for 30 grand?

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.901
[ Laughter ]
Oh!
-Sorry.

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:58.334
[ Cheering and applause ]
I didn't -- I didn't --

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.534
It didn't go through on my Venmo
yet, but it's close, yeah.

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:02.434
It's Venmo.
-Alright, give it time.

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.267
-You've also been
making headlines recently

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:06.534
because someone asked you

00:02:06.534 --> 00:02:08.067
who would you like
to play in a biopic

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:10.534
and you've probably been asked
this a bunch of times

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:13.567
and you were like,
"I don't know, Willie Nelson?"

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:18.767
-Yeah, I thought Willie Nelson
because I think I resemble him.

00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:21.901
I'm old and craggy and...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.901 --> 00:02:23.567
...you know?
So, yeah,

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:25.334
I think I could do
Willie Nelson.

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:27.234
What do you think?
Can I do a Willie?

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:28.501
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:31.000
-But also, the other names --

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.901
the other name that came up
is Gordon Lightfoot.

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:36.834
-Oh, do you remember him?
-Canadian legend.

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:38.000
-Yes.
-Legend!

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.234
[ Cheering and applause ]
Here's Gordon Lightfoot.

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:41.968
[ Whistles ]

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:43.434
-Yeah!
-Oh, yeah!

00:02:43.434 --> 00:02:44.934
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Yeah. Can you do? Yeah.
Can we do?

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:46.367
Yeah, I could see that.

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:48.767
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:49.534
-♪ Sundown ♪

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:51.968
♪ You better take care ♪

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:54.067
♪ If I find
you've been creepin' ♪

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:56.601
♪ round my back stairs ♪

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:58.734
-"Sundown" was a good one.

00:02:58.734 --> 00:02:59.567
♪ Sundown ♪

00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:00.901
And then --

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:04.133
♪ If you could ♪
-♪ Read my mind, love ♪

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:06.067
[ Laughter ]
♪ What a tale
my thoughts would tell ♪

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:07.467
-I'm watching
this movie tomorrow.

00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:08.534
[ Laughter ]
I would watch this tomorrow.

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:11.634
♪ Just like an old-time movie ♪

00:03:11.634 --> 00:03:13.801
-How about --
I'm going into like Bowie.

00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:16.501
-[ As Bowie ]
♪ An old-time movie ♪

00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:17.701
-Another one that came up

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:19.067
that someone said
that you should play

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:20.467
is Stan Lee.

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:21.734
-Oh, from -- yeah, from the --

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.167
[ Cheering and applause ]
Yeah. Yes.

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:27.167
[ Whistling ]

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:28.868
-I actually have --
-Oh.

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:30.734
Stan Lee glasses?
-I have sunglasses,

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:32.167
if you could maybe try --

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:32.868
-Ooh.

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:35.767
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:42.834
Now, this -- I look like
I'm right out of the '70s.

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:44.167
-Yay!

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:45.667
-I'm a porn star, you know.

00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:47.400
[ Laughter ]
How you doing?

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.033
-I like --
-I should be chewing gum.

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:50.234
-I like that look.

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:51.934
[ New York accent ]
Bryan Cranston is here!

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:53.067
-How you doing?
-Hey, how you doing?

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:54.501
-Hey, how you doing?
-How's youse doing?

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:55.934
-Is this guy giving you
a problem?

00:03:55.934 --> 00:03:57.501
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Whoa! Whoa!
-Is this guy --

00:03:57.501 --> 00:03:59.334
this guy here giving you
a problem?

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:01.834
-No problem here.
-I'm just saying.

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:03.400
-We don't want any problem here.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:04.734
-Don't make me do this.

00:04:04.734 --> 00:04:06.400
[ Laughter ]
-How about this?
-I have my tissues.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:07.567
-No, he's got tissues.

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:09.467
No more sneezing.
Allergy season.

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:10.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:12.934
You know what I did have,
though, just in case?

00:04:12.934 --> 00:04:15.334
-What have you got?
You have all kinds of props.

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:17.767
[ Laughter ]
-I'm like I've turned into like
a prop comic here.

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:19.834
I just wanted to see what you
look like as Willie Nelson.

00:04:19.834 --> 00:04:21.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:23.367
Would you do it?

00:04:23.367 --> 00:04:24.400
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Let's do it, okay.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:31.133
♪♪

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:32.200
Oh, that's pretty good.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.000
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.534
[Indistinct]

00:04:35.534 --> 00:04:37.267
[ Whistling ]

00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:39.067
♪♪

00:04:39.067 --> 00:04:39.767
-Yeah!

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:44.801
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:47.534
-♪ To all the girls I've loved ♪

00:04:47.534 --> 00:04:49.200
♪ Before ♪

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:50.667
-Oh, I love -- great!

00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:52.701
♪ Who traveled in and out ♪

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:53.701
-Wait, this is --

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:54.767
[ Laughter ]
-♪ My door ♪

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:56.200
-We'll get a real beard.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.801
When you do the movie.
When you do the movie.

00:04:58.801 --> 00:05:00.868
[ Laughter ]
Yes! Do it like that.
So Willie!

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:02.267
That's so Willie!
-♪ I'm glad they came along ♪

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:03.534
-Willie always did that!

00:05:03.534 --> 00:05:06.133
-♪ I dedicate this song ♪
-Willie always did that.

00:05:06.133 --> 00:05:08.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:09.667
Make that his thing.
That's the thing you do

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:11.067
when you do his biopic,

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:12.834
you make Willie always do this.
-Just always is?

00:05:12.834 --> 00:05:14.734
-He always holds his beard up.

00:05:14.734 --> 00:05:16.200
-Always holds --
-Yeah.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.000
You're the one who's going
to rewrite history

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.901
and tell the story.
-I know. It's fabulous.

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:21.434
-I could see you
as Willie Nelson.
-Could you?

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:24.667
I actual-- I'm not kidding.
I really could see that.

00:05:24.667 --> 00:05:26.467
[ Laughter ]
No. He doesn't do that.

00:05:26.467 --> 00:05:28.901
-He doesn't do that?
-No, he doesn't do that, either.

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:31.834
[ Laughter ]
Can we talk about "Your Honor"?

00:05:31.834 --> 00:05:33.367
-Is it a good look?
Should I keep this look?

00:05:33.367 --> 00:05:35.934
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:38.000
You know what?

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.400
Yeah, I have to ask my wife
on that

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.167
because she's very sensitive

00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:46.133
about the look of the man
she married 35 years ago.

00:05:46.133 --> 00:05:47.534
[ Laughter ]
-But, I mean, look at you

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:49.634
in Season 2, though, of --
-Yeah, that's why.

00:05:49.634 --> 00:05:51.767
-of "Your Honor."

00:05:51.767 --> 00:05:53.200
This is you. This is --

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.801
Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:54.801 --> 00:05:56.868
[ Cheering and applause ]
-That's a look right there, bud.

00:05:56.868 --> 00:06:01.734
-I can't -- my wife absolutely
refused to have, uh,

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:04.033
relations with me, shall we say?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:05.234
-I love how you
censored yourself.

00:06:05.234 --> 00:06:07.534
Thank you so much.
Thank you so much.

00:06:07.534 --> 00:06:08.767
Yes, I understand
what you're saying.

00:06:08.767 --> 00:06:10.300
-Yes.
-She refused.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.834
[ Laughter ]
-She refused. She said,
"I'm not going to --

00:06:12.834 --> 00:06:14.501
No, I'm not going to go
to bed with that."

00:06:14.501 --> 00:06:16.400
-Wow!
-That's not a thing.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.234
Will you go to bed --
My wife is in the audience.

00:06:18.234 --> 00:06:19.868
Will you go to bed with this?
-Yeah!

00:06:19.868 --> 00:06:21.167
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:21.167 --> 00:06:22.367
She's somewhere.
Where is she?

00:06:22.367 --> 00:06:24.300
-She says yes. She says yes.
-Alright, good.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.167
-But also,
you had a pretty interesting --

00:06:26.167 --> 00:06:28.167
a little trivia
about your beard here.

00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:30.734
-Oh, well, I was going
to shave it off earlier,

00:06:30.734 --> 00:06:32.834
but I found a nest in there.

00:06:32.834 --> 00:06:34.234
[ Laughter ]
These birds.

00:06:34.234 --> 00:06:36.033
They were such darling
little birds,

00:06:36.033 --> 00:06:37.968
I didn't have the heart to.
-Yeah, a bird was nesting

00:06:37.968 --> 00:06:39.200
in there. There's a little home
there, yeah.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.901
-They weren't ready to fly off,
so I kept it.

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:45.501
-There's one episode left
of "Your Honor."

00:06:45.501 --> 00:06:48.067
How do we set it up
for anyone who hasn't --

00:06:48.067 --> 00:06:49.334
What do we have to expect?

00:06:49.334 --> 00:06:50.901
-Well, as long as I can,

00:06:50.901 --> 00:06:53.167
you know,
relay this very seriously.

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:55.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.801
It's a very serious show.
-I forgot to ask you to take --

00:06:57.801 --> 00:06:59.100
Would you like
to take that wig off?

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:00.334
-I don't know.
I'm getting kind of used to it.

00:07:00.334 --> 00:07:01.868
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, I kind of like it.

00:07:01.868 --> 00:07:04.834
Talk to me about "Your Honor."
This is the season finale.

00:07:04.834 --> 00:07:06.501
-It's --
You know, I didn't think

00:07:06.501 --> 00:07:08.334
there was enough anguish
in the world, Jimmy.

00:07:08.334 --> 00:07:10.534
I wanted to bring more --

00:07:10.534 --> 00:07:13.701
more tension and stress
to people's lives,

00:07:13.701 --> 00:07:14.901
[ Laughter ]
so, I made --

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:17.868
No, after the tragedy
at the end of "Season 1."

00:07:17.868 --> 00:07:19.801
-It was so good.
-Oh, thank you.

00:07:19.801 --> 00:07:24.133
I wanted to give
the audience a little break

00:07:24.133 --> 00:07:27.200
and to see some measure of hope.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:30.501
I also wanted to explore
what it's like, honestly,

00:07:30.501 --> 00:07:33.167
to deal with grief and despair.

00:07:33.167 --> 00:07:34.868
And then the last thing was,

00:07:34.868 --> 00:07:37.467
is there redemption
in our lives now?

00:07:37.467 --> 00:07:39.234
Can someone redeem themselves?

00:07:39.234 --> 00:07:45.567
Can you seek forgiveness
and can you grant forgiveness?

00:07:45.567 --> 00:07:48.467
And I think it's a strength
of human character

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:50.167
to be able to say you're sorry,

00:07:50.167 --> 00:07:54.033
to be able to forget
and forgive.

00:07:54.033 --> 00:07:55.567
-Forgive.
-I think it's
an important thing.

00:07:55.567 --> 00:07:58.367
-Yeah. Absolutely,
I think it is, too.

00:07:58.367 --> 00:07:59.534
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Is it the hair?

00:07:59.534 --> 00:08:01.667
-It's perfect.

00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:03.033
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:03.033 --> 00:08:05.033
Here's Bryan Cranston
in "Your Honor."

00:08:05.033 --> 00:08:07.100
Take a look at this.

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:08.734
-Adam fell to the floor.

00:08:10.534 --> 00:08:14.000
I ran inside
and I-I yelled for help.

00:08:17.868 --> 00:08:21.934
I held my son
in my arms as he died.

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:24.534
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:27.400
-Did you see who shot him?

00:08:29.567 --> 00:08:31.634
-Yes.

00:08:31.634 --> 00:08:34.100
-And was it the defendant,
Eugene Jones?

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:40.667
♪♪

00:08:40.667 --> 00:08:41.567
-Yes, it was.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.267
[ Spectators murmuring ]

00:08:47.868 --> 00:08:49.400
-Ooh!

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:52.167
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:08:52.167 --> 00:08:54.601
The Season 2 finale --

00:08:56.634 --> 00:09:00.300
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:01.601
The Season 2 finale

00:09:01.601 --> 00:09:04.467
of "Your Honor" comes
to Showtime this weekend!

00:09:04.467 --> 00:09:06.901
More with Bryan Cranston
when we come back.

00:09:06.901 --> 00:09:07.968
Stick around, everybody.

